
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C E F : Points
B,C,A are collinear [00]
E,C,B are collinear [01]
EC = EB [02]
EF = EC [03]
AF ⟂ EF [04]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
G : Points
G,A,F are collinear [05]

 * Proof steps:
001. EF = EC [03] ⇒  ∠EFC = ∠FCE [06]
002. EF = EC [03] & EC = EB [02] ⇒  E is the circumcenter of \Delta FCB [07]
003. G,F,A are collinear [05] & EF ⟂ AF [04] ⇒  EF ⟂ FG [08]
004. E is the circumcenter of \Delta FCB [07] & EF ⟂ FG [08] ⇒  ∠GFC = ∠FBC [09]
005. ∠EFC = ∠FCE [06] & E,C,B are collinear [01] & B,C,A are collinear [00] & ∠GFC = ∠FBC [09] & G,A,F are collinear [05] ⇒  ∠BFA = ∠CFE
